language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ session1_bank_card: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ A bank card has a 4-digit PIN abcd. No two digits are the same, the 2-digit number cd is 3 times the 2-digit
$ number ab, and the 2-digit number da is 2 times the 2-digit number bc. Find the PIN.
$
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/session1_bank_card.html
$ Save this model as model.eprime and run it with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the solution is
$ written to `model.eprime.solution`:
$   savilerow model.eprime -run-solver

$ a: first digit of the PIN (nonzero, as the PIN has 4 digits)
find a : int(0..9)
$ b: second digit of the PIN
find b : int(0..9)
$ c: third digit of the PIN
find c : int(0..9)
$ d: fourth digit of the PIN
find d : int(0..9)

such that
$ no two digits are the same
allDiff([a, b, c, d]),
$ the PIN has 4 digits, so the first one is not zero
a != 0,
$ the 2-digit number cd is 3 times the 2-digit number ab
10*c + d = 3 * (10*a + b),
$ the 2-digit number da is 2 times the 2-digit number bc
10*d + a = 2 * (10*b + c)
